Task: Park mission FSM + respond tap (FR2, FR5)

Summary: new src/game/mission/parkMission.ts - pure FSM mirroring
missionManager/iceCreamMission: idle -> spawn() -> spawned ->
respond() -> responding <-> collecting (COLLECT_RANGE 1.9, the shared
mission range) -> finish() -> complete -> ~2.5s linger -> idle.
Driving away only disarms collecting, never cancels (NFR1); spawn
ignored while running; finish() only bites once the kid has answered
and only once. resolveParkTap({state, onPiece}) sits beside
resolveOrderTap: 'respond' only for a piece tap while spawned, so the
morph + drive fire exactly once.

Why: FR2/FR5 - the FSM owns the errand's shape while parkPickup.ts
(FR3/FR4) owns collection; completion is reported by the pickup rules
via finish(), not by the FSM counting pieces.

Tests: parkMission.test.ts (9, red first): full chain to idle, spawn
ignored while running, distance never jumps the gun in spawned,
respond-once via resolveParkTap, miss/quiet-town taps ignore,
collecting disarms to responding and re-arms, linger ~2.5s, negative
frame ignored, finish only after respond and only once.

Note: one red-phase assertion was corrected before green - it called
